Proposed Modules & Implementation Details
1. Multi-Database & Multi-Source Connector Layer (src/connectors/)
•	base.py: Generic Abstract Connector defining unified methods: fetch_dataframe(query_or_table, params, chunksize), fetch_aggregates(table, group_by, metrics), get_row_count(table_or_query, filter_expr), get_schema(table_or_query), get_distinct_values(table, column).
•	sqlalchemy_connector.py: Connects to any SQL dialect via SQLAlchemy (SQLite, DuckDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server, Oracle, Snowflake).
•	excel_connector.py: Connects to Excel sheets (.xlsx, .xls) with sheet-as-table abstraction and SQL-like querying via pandas/SQLite memory engine.
•	csv_connector.py: Connects to CSV/TSV/Parquet directories or files.
•	factory.py: Instantiates the appropriate connector from connection URI / YAML config.
2. Star Schema & Data Warehouse Modeling (src/warehouse/)
•	Dimensions (dim_*):
•	dim_date: Generated calendar date dimension (Date_Key YYYYMMDD, Year, Quarter, Month, Month_Name, Week, Day_Of_Week, Is_Weekend, Fiscal_Period).
•	dim_plant: Plant_Key (SK), Plant_Code (BK), Plant_Name, Country, Region, City, Plant_Type, Square_Footage, ISO certifications, Coordinates.
•	dim_production_line: Line_Key (SK), Line_ID (BK), Plant_Code, Line_Name, Line_Type, Automation_Level, Capacity, Safety_Rating.
•	dim_product: Product_Key (SK), Product_SKU (BK), Product_Family, Product_Name, Revision, BOM_Version, Category, Standard_Weight, Target_Cpk.
•	dim_machine: Machine_Key (SK), Machine_ID (BK), Line_ID, Machine_Type, Manufacturer, Model_Year, PLC_Firmware, Criticality.
•	dim_operator: Operator_Key (SK), Operator_ID (BK), Operator_Name, Department, Job_Title, Shift, Labor_Rate.
•	dim_supplier: Supplier_Key (SK), Supplier_ID (BK), Supplier_Name, Country, Tier, Preferred_Status, Quality_Rating.
•	dim_material: Material_Key (SK), Material_ID (BK), Raw_Material_Type, Lot_Number, Storage_Condition, Recycled_Content_Pct.
•	dim_defect_catalog: Defect_Key (SK), Primary_Defect_Type, Secondary_Defect_Type, Critical_Defect_Flag.
•	Fact Tables (fact_*):
•	fact_work_orders: Grain = 1 row per Work Order. Measures: Planned_Qty, Produced_Qty, Good_Qty, Scrap_Qty, Yield_Percent, Cycle_Time, OEE_Percent, Availability, Performance, Quality_Rate.
•	fact_machine_telemetry: Grain = 1 row per Reading. Measures: Spindle_Speed_RPM, Feed_Rate, Tool_Wear_Percent, Coolant_Flow, Temperatures, Vibration, Power_Consumption_kWh, Data_Quality_Score.
•	fact_quality_inspections: Grain = 1 row per Quality Inspection & Measurement. Measures: Sample_Size, Defect_Count, Inspection_Duration_Min, Hardness, Tensile_Strength, SPC_Cpk, SPC_Ppk.
•	fact_labor_performance: Grain = 1 row per Shift Labor. Measures: Hours_Worked, Overtime_Hours, Labor_Rate, Efficiency_Percent.
•	fact_cost_financials: Grain = 1 row per Cost Ledger. Measures: Material_Cost, Labor_Cost, Overhead_Cost, Standard_Cost, Variance, Selling_Price, Gross_Margin_Percent.
•	fact_procurement: Grain = 1 row per Purchase Order. Measures: Order_Qty, Unit_Price, Total_PO_Value, Freight_Cost, Customs_Duty.
3. Data Scaling Engine (src/scaling/)
•	Generates synthetic scaled manufacturing datasets (10k, 100k, 1M rows) scaling from seed excel data.
•	Ensures strict referential integrity (foreign keys properly reference parent dimension entities).
•	Uses realistic statistical distributions, temporal sequences, and correlated metrics (e.g. scrap rates, cycle times, power consumption).
4. Warehouse Migration Pipeline (src/warehouse/migration_pipeline.py)
•	Extracts raw tables from Excel/DB sources.
•	Assigns surrogate keys and builds dimension reference maps.
•	Computes fact table foreign keys via dimension lookups.
•	Bulk loads into Target DWH (manufacturing_dwh.db).
5. Generic Multi-Database Reconciliation Engine (src/reconciliation/)
Supports any source vs any target with dynamic mapping configurations:
•	Module 1: Data Volume Reconciliation
•	Total row counts across source & target.
•	Partition / Group-By volume comparisons (e.g. record counts per Plant, per Month, per Shift).
•	Identification of missing primary/business keys in source or target.
•	Module 2: Data Reconciliation & Attribute-Level Validation
•	Dynamic column mapping (1-to-1, renamed, typed, or transformed).
•	100% cell-by-cell comparison.
•	Absolute (atol) and relative (rtol) numerical tolerance comparison for floats.
•	Case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed string comparison.
•	Standardized Date/Timestamp comparison.
•	Exact mismatch records generation with coordinates [Key, Column, Source_Value, Target_Value, Delta, Delta_Pct].
•	Module 3: Aggregate Measure Reconciliation
•	Compares mathematical aggregations (SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, STDDEV, COUNT) across all key business metrics.
•	Dimensional grouped aggregate checks (e.g. Total Labor Cost by Department, Total Scrap Qty by Plant).
•	Arithmetic integrity checks (e.g. Good_Qty + Scrap_Qty == Produced_Qty).
•	Module 4: Multi-Source Consistency Assessment
•	Flat table (Manufacturing_Data) vs Relational 3NF sheets vs Star Schema Data Warehouse.
•	Validates that no data is lost or corrupted across transformations.
6. Automated Reporting Engine (src/reporting/)
•	Interactive HTML Report: Standalone dashboard with glassmorphism UI, interactive KPI cards, pass/fail badges, Chart.js aggregate comparison charts, and searchable, paginated mismatch drill-down tables.
•	Multi-Tab Excel Workbook: Formatted Excel report (Mismatch_Report.xlsx) with tabs for Executive_Summary, Volume_Reconciliation, Attribute_Mismatches, Aggregate_Reconciliation, and Multi_Source_Consistency.
•	Markdown & JSON Reports: Terminal and CI/CD-friendly outputs with status exit codes.
